{"term":"mundane","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:c39e01acafd6a610b0","definition":"Worldly, earthly, profane, vulgar as opposed to heavenly.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["profane","temporal","worldly","areligious","civil","earthly","irreligious","laicist","laicistic","mundane","nonreligious","profane","secular","temporal","unconsecrated","unsanctified","worldly"],"antonyms":["heavenly","arcane"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antemundane","circummundane","extramundane","inframundane","intermundane","intramundane","mundania","mundanism","mundie","nonmundane","submundane","supermundane","supramundane","transmundane","ultramundane","unmundane"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mundane#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ebc81766c3f53c7250","definition":"Pertaining to the Universe, cosmos or physical reality, as opposed to the spiritual world.","example":"Amongst mundane bodies, six there are that do perpetually move, and they are the six Planets; of the rest, that is, of the Earth, Sun, and fixed Stars, it is disputable which of them moveth, and which stands still.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antemundane","circummundane","extramundane","inframundane","intermundane","intramundane","mundania","mundanism","mundie","nonmundane","submundane","supermundane","supramundane","transmundane","ultramundane","unmundane"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mundane#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3aefbd71d1bc62ee1c","definition":"Ordinary; not new; part of the mainstream culture.","example":"THE LIVERPOOL PARTY at Pat and Frank Milnes’ celebrated both the Gunpowder Plot and the Liverpool Club’s 400th and something meeting. Two mundane and non-fan friends